#
# prima-materia — the searches of the run on the Platform Sūtra, 2026-10-14
#
# In a file of their own for the mechanical reason recorded at
# examinations/searches-jain.ttl and in prima-materia#703.
#

pmp:ChanWeixianSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Every caution, danger and named failure in the Platform Sūtra"@en, "Jede Warnung, Gefahr und benannte Misslingensform im Plattform-Sūtra"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Liuzu dashi fabao tanjing, Zongbao recension, T48 no. 2008, chapters 1 to 10 read complete in the Chinese; every passage found checked in the Dunhuang text, T48 no. 2007, and in the translations of Thomas Cleary (1998) and of the Buddhist Text Translation Society (3rd ed. 2001)."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "Any statement that a practice taught or reported in the work can go wrong, harm the practitioner, bind him, or fail to bring about what it is practised for, and any account of why it failed."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "In the Chinese: 病, 顛, 狂, 縛, 繫縛, 障, 邪, 迷, 死, 無情, 無記空, 不悟, 不見性, 無益, 不得, 救不可得, 慎勿, 莫, 勿, 若違; in the English of both translations at the same places: sick, sickness, pathological, insane, delusional, bondage, bind, obstruct, wrong view, deluded, dead, insentient, no benefit."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:ChanKanxinChengDian, pmc:ChanChangzuoTongWuqing, pmc:ChanKongxinJingzuo, pmc:ChanBaiwuBusi, pmc:ChanZhuoJingJingFu, pmc:ChanZhuxinGuanjingShiBing, pmc:ChanKounianXinbuxing, pmc:ChanXiaogenBuWu, pmc:ChanYanxiaBuWu, pmc:ChanJiuXiuBuWu ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-14" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-14" ;
    skos:note "Six cautions and four named failures. All six cautions are against one way of sitting, the watching of the mind and of stillness, and the two that state bodily consequences, madness and death on the cutting off of thought, are both in the Dunhuang text. The four failures are all states of the practitioner without an outward mark: recitation that stayed in the mouth, small faculties, not awakening at the words, and long practice in the wrong method."@en .

pmp:ChanJianyanSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the Platform Sūtra gives any act or sign by which another can tell that someone has seen the nature"@en, "Ob das Plattform-Sūtra eine Handlung oder ein Zeichen nennt, an dem ein anderer erkennen kann, dass jemand die Natur gesehen hat"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "The same work in the same witnesses, the Chinese read complete."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "Any test, examination, verdict or sign perceptible to someone other than the practitioner that decides whether seeing the nature has happened, and any statement that it cannot be decided from outside."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "In the Chinese: 驗, 試, 看, 呈, 偈, 見性, 未見, 門外, 門前, 印可, 證, 自知, 冷暖, 聲, 瑞, 相; in the English at the same places: test, show, verse, seen the nature, not yet, gate, certify, seal, knows for himself, sign, voice."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:ChanJiekanYan, pmc:ChanLengnuanZizhi, pmc:ChanKongzhongYouSheng ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-14" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-14" ;
    skos:note "One assay, one public sign and one counter-principle. The assay by verse has a failing verdict and a stated criterion, but the work records the examiner giving a false public verdict on purpose. The sign, a voice in the sky naming the man, is in the later recension only and attaches to one case. The counter-principle, that one knows for oneself as one knows water cold or warm and that one person's seeing cannot settle another's, stands beside the assay unreconciled."@en .

pmp:ChanQixianSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the Platform Sūtra names a term, a count of attempts or a condition under which practice is to be given up"@en, "Ob das Plattform-Sūtra eine Frist, eine Zahl von Versuchen oder eine Bedingung nennt, unter der die Übung aufzugeben ist"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "The same work in the same witnesses, the Chinese read complete."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "A term in days or years after which seeing the nature is to be expected, a number of attempts after which nothing more is to be expected, or an instruction to stop."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "In the Chinese: 年, 載, 日, 度, 遍, 劫, 時, 久, 捨, 止, 休, 罷, 退, 不可得; in the English at the same places: years, days, times, kalpas, long, give up, stop, abandon, in vain."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-14" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-14" ;
    skos:note "Nothing. The work counts years and attempts of failed practice, thirteen approaches, three thousand recitations, a thousand readings, nine, ten and twenty years, entered at pmc:ChanJiuXiuBuWu; but none of these counts is a rule, none of the six is told to stop, and the remedy in every case is a change of method at a teacher's words. The only term in the work is the ten thousand kalpas in which mouth recitation without the mind does not see the nature, which is a statement that the method fails and not a term after which to judge it."@en .
